<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gangaikondacholapuram</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gangaikondacholapuram, &quot;city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> who took the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>&quot;, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, was founded by the Chola king Rajendra I around 1025 to celebrate his northern campaign to the Ganges. It served as the Chola capital for about 250 years. Its great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a> temple survives and forms part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> of the Great Living Chola Temples, while the city itself is now a village.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gangaikondacholapuram.jpg" alt="Gangaikondacholapuram" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ssriraman · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GangaiKonda_Cholapuram(Front_View).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
